## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical blind-source separation in a realistic, asynchronous sensor network with nonstationary mixing, clock drift, and dropout.

## Key Concepts
- Online whitening with forgetting factor across heterogeneous sensors
- Trade-offs: per-bin ICA vs joint diagonalization in mixed-quality data
- Robust update rules for missing data and dropout
- Ground-truth injection for evaluation (SDR/SIR, tolerance to drift)

